# What a machine takes from this repository when it has no rows of its own, as piece | value.
#
# Every piece here is one optional piece. Its row says what a machine gets by default, and the
# reason after it says what the piece brings. Everything not listed here is core and every
# machine takes it. A machine writes a row in machines/<name>/pieces only where it differs from
# the default. The directory is named by `scutil --get LocalHostName`, and MDJ_MACHINE answers for
# it in a run that should pretend to be another machine. `default` is never a machine name.
#
# README.md, under "Capturing a machine", has the steps to add or update a machine, and
# `src/machine.sh capture` writes its pieces file. src/machine.sh is the only reader. setup.sh,
# the stow step, the Brewfile and the reconciler all ask it, and nothing else knows this layout.
# decisions/machine-profiles.md has why machines are data and not one branch per machine.
#
# The defaults keep what every machine got before this directory existed, except mise, which
# stays off unless a machine asks, since a machine with its own pyenv or nvm must not be taken over.

# piece        | value      # reason
mise           | off       # the mise package, its Homebrew line, the runtime install step, and the shell activation that follows the stowed config
hammerspoon    | on        # the Hammerspoon package and cask, and the Caps Lock remap its Hyper key stands on
herdr          | on        # the herdr package and formula, and the step that registers its plugin
mole           | on        # the mole formula, the package itself is not stowed yet
docker         | on        # the Docker Desktop cask
vpn            | mullvad   # mullvad, ivpn or none, and only ivpn adds a setup step, the permission repair its daemon needs
tools          | none      # the mise tools a machine takes, names from dotfiles/mise/TOOLS, comma separated, alphabetical, no spaces, or none
